==English==

===Etymology===
From ''[[en-]]'' + ''[[life]]'' + ''[[-en]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/ɛnˈlaɪv.ən/}}
*:Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-aɪvən|-aɪvən]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|obsolete|transitive}} To give [[life]] or [[spirit]] to; to [[revive]] or [[animate]].
# {{transitive}} To make more [[lively]], [[cheerful]] or [[interesting]].
#: ''The game was much '''enlivened''' when both teams scored within five minutes of each other.''

